# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: wamm-error-buffer-once
why: Init() calls InitErrorMessageBuffer(), which mallocs the global error-message buffer again on every hash and
why: drops the previous one (LeakSanitizer, CI run 45581879065). The patch allocates it only while it is NULL;
why: it is still cleared on every call, so the observable behaviour is unchanged.
file: upstream/WaMM/Reference_Implementation/WaMM_Ref/WaMM_Ref/WaMMErrorMessage.c
count: 1
find: 	_WaMM_ErrorMesssage = (char*) malloc(WaMM_ErrorMessageBufferSize);
replace: 	if (_WaMM_ErrorMesssage == NULL) _WaMM_ErrorMesssage = (char*) malloc(WaMM_ErrorMessageBufferSize);
